WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:04.146
More years passed.

2
00:00:04.147 --> 00:00:07.570
The prince often walked in the forest.

3
00:00:07.571 --> 00:00:13.405
Sometimes his servant walked with him.

4
00:00:13.406 --> 00:00:17.531
"Can we please go?" his servant moaned.

5
00:00:17.532 --> 00:00:20.091
"It's cold and dark!

6
00:00:20.092 --> 00:00:23.721
There are sharp thorns everywhere."

7
00:00:23.722 --> 00:00:26.954
"Shh!" the prince said.

8
00:00:26.955 --> 00:00:30.193
"I hear that lovely voice again.

9
00:00:30.194 --> 00:00:33.597
I must find the singer!"

10
00:00:33.598 --> 00:00:37.763
"Look!" the servant said suddenly.

11
00:00:37.764 --> 00:00:44.434
An old witch was flying through the trees.

12
00:00:44.435 --> 00:00:53.645
"What are you doing in this forest?" she yelled.

13
00:00:53.646 --> 00:00:57.165
The prince stared at her.

14
00:00:57.166 --> 00:01:01.175
"The witch from the market!" he thought.

15
00:01:01.176 --> 00:01:06.066
The prince waved. "You have your flying shawl.

16
00:01:06.067 --> 00:01:08.979
Can you make one for me?"

17
00:01:08.980 --> 00:01:14.221
"No!" the witch said. "It's a hard spell.

18
00:01:14.222 --> 00:01:16.837
It takes months and—"

19
00:01:16.838 --> 00:01:19.478
"Be careful!" the prince said.

20
00:01:19.479 --> 00:01:24.006
Crash! The witch fell in a thornbush.

21
00:01:24.007 --> 00:01:29.245
"Ouch!" she yelled.

22
00:01:29.246 --> 00:01:33.373
The prince lifted the witch from the thornbush.

23
00:01:33.374 --> 00:01:36.443
He tried to remove her shawl next.

24
00:01:36.444 --> 00:01:40.666
But it was stuck to the thorns.

25
00:01:40.667 --> 00:01:47.112
Finally the witch yanked it from the bush.

26
00:01:47.113 --> 00:01:50.045
"My shawl is ruined!

27
00:01:50.046 --> 00:01:53.035
Now I cannot fly for months.

28
00:01:53.036 --> 00:01:56.433
This is your fault!"

29
00:01:56.434 --> 00:01:59.433
"I'm sorry," the prince said.

30
00:01:59.434 --> 00:02:02.198
"You can ride my horse instead.

31
00:02:02.199 --> 00:02:05.345
And I can carry your heavy basket.

32
00:02:05.346 --> 00:02:08.112
Where are you going?"

33
00:02:08.113 --> 00:02:11.411
"Nowhere!" the witch shouted.

34
00:02:11.412 --> 00:02:13.889
"Leave me alone!"

35
00:02:13.890 --> 00:02:18.580
She stuffed the ripped shawl into her basket.

36
00:02:18.581 --> 00:02:22.251
She stomped off through the trees.

37
00:02:22.252 --> 00:02:28.347
The servant sighed. "Can we go now?"

38
00:02:28.348 --> 00:02:32.276
The prince watched the witch leave.

39
00:02:32.277 --> 00:02:37.406
Suddenly he remembered the girl with the long hair.

40
00:02:37.407 --> 00:02:43.313
"No!" he said. "Let's follow that witch!"

41
00:02:43.314 --> 00:02:48.346
In the tower Rapunzel was waiting for the witch.

42
00:02:48.347 --> 00:02:52.005
"She is late today," Rapunzel thought.

43
00:02:52.006 --> 00:02:54.969
"I wonder where she is."

44
00:02:54.970 --> 00:02:57.718
Finally she heard a sound.

45
00:02:57.719 --> 00:03:04.128
"I'm down here!" the witch yelled.

46
00:03:04.129 --> 00:03:07.226
"My flying shawl is ruined.

47
00:03:07.227 --> 00:03:11.594
I cannot get into the tower!"

